# Chase work loop (discuss → author → main)

When this Cursor chat is the Sume **main agent** with Chase, default to this
loop. Policy SoT (do not fork forever):
`~/.agents/skills/sume-main-agent-orchestration/SKILL.md`
§ "Chase work loop — discuss → lock → mega-issue → author → main".

Opus Shell recipe: `~/.cursor/rules/opus-background-terminal.mdc`.
Graphite enqueue/land ops: `~/.agents/skills/sume-gt-mq/SKILL.md` (required
before any `gt submit` / `gt merge`).

## What this is

Chase and main **talk first** (intent, naming, defaults, non-goals), then main
**files a durable issue** and **hands implementation to the author worker**.
That worker **lands to `origin/main`**. Main does not silently become the
sole implementer for work Chase expected on that flow.

## Roles

| Who | Owns |
|-----|------|
| Chase | Product locks, “go / defer” |
| Main (this chat) | Discuss (match Chase’s language), survey, issue, launch workers, **self-contained chat report** (Slack is a mirror) |
| Opus | **Default author** if Chase did not name a model. BP → fresh clone → `gt submit` → tip `merge-queue` → **stay until `origin/main` `(#N)`** |
| Fable | Author **only** when Chase said Fable. Same path through main tip. |
| Astra / Codex | Author when Chase named them. Same path through main tip. |
| Grok | Author **only** when Chase said Grok. Same path through main tip. Never default MQ babysit. Never Cursor `Task`. |
| Composer | Explore only |

**Default author = Opus.** **Default land owner = that same author**
(Chase lock 2026-09-06). Forbidden: `HANDOFF: grok-land`.

## Step-by-step

### 1) Discuss
- Clarify outcome, surfaces (UI/docs/API), and what must *not* change.
- Light code/docs peeks OK; do not start a parallel full implementation.
- User-facing replies: **same language as Chase’s latest message** (usually Korean).

### 2) Lock
Capture in issue/BP, not chat memory only:
- Product nouns / defaults / wire vs chrome splits
- Non-goals and “Needs verification”
- Author owns land to main (default). Do not split enqueue vs Grok land.
- Dev-only unless Chase authorizes prod

### 3) Mega-issue
- Prefer `/github-mega-issue` / `github-mega-issue` skill.
- Self-contained enough that the author needs no prior transcript.
- Clear/small: main may write the issue. Heavy design: Opus may draft issue then implement (Pipeline 1).
- Create when Chase said to file / “그렇게 가보자” on that flow — not a silent draft-only unless they asked for a draft first.

### 4) Hand to author
Pick a **job slug** first (2–4 kebab tokens, aim for 3). Optional issue suffix only
(`…-2000`). Never `--name 2000` alone.

**Terminal + board title (required):** Shell `description` (and Active
workers board Job column) must be:

`Opus : <job-slug> (#<issue>)` (or `Astra :` / `Fable :` / `Grok :` if named)

Prompt must include issue URL, locks, **`sume-gt-mq` required-skill line**,
the **GRAPHITE hard-lock** from `GRAPHITE-HARD-LOCK.md` (author stays to
main tip). Stage: BP → `cstack-clone` → implement → `gt create` →
`gt submit` → `cstack-gt-wait-merge` → **stay until `origin/main` `(#N)`**.
Forbidden: `HANDOFF: grok-land`, `gh pr create`, `move_agent_to_root`.

### 5) Tell Chase (short)
- Issue URL, title `Opus : <job-slug> (#N)`, `session_id=…`
- Do **not** poll; completion notification is the monitor

### 6) On author completion notification
1. Read `—— final ——` (+ `session_id`) only.
2. Brief status in Chase’s language.
3. If they exited at enqueue (`LANDED: no`): **resume the same session**
   with stay-until-main. Do **not** launch Grok land.
4. Say **완료** to Chase only after `origin/main` `(#N)`.

### 7) Residuals
Leave issue OPEN with an explicit residual, or close when AC met.

## Phrase triggers (run this loop)

- “mega-issue → opus”, “/github-mega-issue”, “BP → PR”, “플로우 타자”
- “그렇게 가보자” after a product lock discussion

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Do instead |
|-----|------------|
| Main implements the whole feature Chase meant for Opus | Issue → author |
| Author STOP after `merge-queue` / `HANDOFF: grok-land` | Same session until main tip |
| Launch Grok land after enqueue | Resume the author if they left early |
| Tell Chase 완료 on enqueue / green CI / “Your changes” | 완료 only after `origin/main` `(#N)` |
| `gh pr create` | Fresh clone → `gt create` → `gt submit` |
| Endless `gh run rerun` | ≤2 reruns → minimal CI unblock |

## Parallel trains

Multiple job slugs OK. Note rebase risk when trains touch the same paths.
